{{~##
   What every generated Ruby file starts with: the banner, the requires and the module.

   Ruby has no autoloader here, so a split file requires what it uses - and how deep it sits
   decides the path. Both are worked out in the generator, because path arithmetic in a
   template is arithmetic nothing can test.

   The module is reopened in every file rather than nested from one place. That is how Ruby
   works: `module X` opens X whether or not something else already did.
##~}}
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated by Tabbit. DO NOT EDIT.
#
# Changes to this file may cause incorrect behavior and will be lost if the code is
# regenerated.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
{{~ for line in requires }}
require_relative '{{ line }}'
{{~ end }}

module {{ module_name }}
